 "question": "What was the calendar-year 2024 combined ratio (reported loss, change in IBNR, paid ALAE and expenses, over earned premium)?",
 "final_text": "The 2024 combined ratio is about **1.073** (1.0726).\n\n**Build-up (calendar year 2024, GBP):**\n- **Reported loss, net:** \u00a320,037,477 (indemnity payments \u00a316,729,867, plus case reserve movements \u00a33,842,954, less recoveries \u00a3535,344).\n- **Paid ALAE:** \u00a3894,254.\n- **Change in IBNR:** \u00a31,171,389. This is the all-accident-year total at 31 Dec 2024 (\u00a34,562,282) less the total at 31 Dec 2023 (\u00a33,390,893).\n- **Expenses:** \u00a33,365,614 (acquisition, commission and admin, by expense month).\n- **Total:** \u00a325,468,734.\n- **Earned premium:** \u00a323,744,583. Each premium transaction (new, renewal, mid-term adjustment, cancellation) is pro-rated over its cover period by days falling in 2024.\n\nRatio: 25,468,734 / 23,744,583 = 1.0726.\n\nExpenses are assigned by expense month rather than booked date. Booked-date timing would shift a few hundred thousand pounds between years.\n\nANSWER: 1.0726",
 "stop_reason": "end_turn",
